1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,620
Imagine a sales rep making a great customer call.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:06,100
A transcript captures the conversation, but the rep still

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,580
copies notes into a record by hand.

4
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:11,480
Across a thousand reps, the calls keep coming.

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:15,200
The account executive asks for context, the manager chases

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,540
targets, and manual handoffs become the bottleneck.

7
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:22,580
A good call should not end in missing information.

8
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,380
This pipeline applies a pattern from my production experience.

9
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:30,640
In Slack, Sam asks for available skills.

10
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:34,320
The app checks access and privately returns the permitted

11
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:34,780
tasks.

12
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:37,040
A teammate sees fewer skills.

13
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:40,440
Call review is missing, and requesting it directly is

14
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:40,780
denied.

15
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:43,620
Sam sends the transcript for review.

16
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:47,160
Slack confirms it is queued, while the work continues

17
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:47,860
in the background.

18
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,640
The app verifies the signed Slack request.

19
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:53,720
A queue hands it to a worker, which rechecks

20
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,160
access and starts the Python workflow.

21
00:00:56,680 --> 00:01:00,120
AWS AgentCore Runtime hosts that workflow.

22
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:03,860
It loads the selected skill instructions from S3, which

23
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:05,900
tell the language model what to extract.

24
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,100
Nova proposes facts, then Python calls tools through the

25
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,040
MCP gateway.

26
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:14,500
The tools check permission and evidence before saving the

27
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,180
shared record in DynamoDB.

28
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:19,460
The worker saves the result and replies in Slack

29
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:21,040
with the checked stage and amount.

30
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:24,540
A separate meeting prep command reads those saved facts

31
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:27,120
before the model drafts a brief, so the next

32
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:29,980
teammate gets shared context without another handoff.

33
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,060
Let the sales organization do what it does best:

34
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:34,400
win sales for you.
